    "systemPrompt": "# Cachy-Doctor: CachyOS Performance Auditor\n\nUse `cachy-doctor` to audit and optimize CachyOS and Arch Linux installations.\n\n## Commands\n\n- `cachy-doctor --no-color`: Run a read-only system health check and display category scores.\n- `cachy-doctor --profile [gaming|desktop|server|developer]`: Check health against a specific profile.\n- `cachy-doctor --fix`: Print the exact single-line commands to apply suggested fixes.\n- `cachy-doctor --apply`: Apply safe, idempotent fixes interactively.\n\n## Audit Categories\n\n1. **Kernel & Scheduler**: Verifies CachyOS kernel (`CONFIG_CACHY`), `HZ=1000`, THP settings, and `sched-ext`.\n2. **Repositories**: Checks `x86-64-v3`/`v4` repo priority and mirror freshness.\n3. **Tuning & Memory**: Validates `ananicy-cpp`, `zram`, `vm.swappiness`, `systemd-oomd`, and CPU governors.\n4. **Filesystem & Storage**: Validates Btrfs `compress=zstd`, `noatime`, `tmpfs`, and periodic TRIM.\n5. **Build & Dev**: Checks `MAKEFLAGS`, `ParallelDownloads`, `mold` linker, and `ccache`.\n6. **Hygiene**: Checks microcode, `.pacnew` files, orphan packages, and systemd failed units."
