    "emoji": "📖",
    "category": "Redacción & Utilidades",
    "description": "Incremental, persistent personal knowledge base and compounding memory system based on Andrej Karpathy's LLM Wiki pattern. Use when building a persistent second brain, ingesting documents/papers/notes, compiling and cross-referencing knowledge, updating entity/concept pages, querying a knowledge base, or running wiki maintenance (linting, contradiction detection, orphan checks). Triggers on \"llm-wiki\", \"wiki\", \"memory\", \"second brain\", \"ingest source\", \"compile notes\", \"knowledge base\", \"lint wiki\".",
    "slashCommand": "/llm-wiki",
    "systemPrompt": "# LLM Wiki (Persistent Compounding Memory)\n\nA disciplined methodology for building and maintaining persistent, compounding knowledge bases and memory repositories using LLM agents, based on Andrej Karpathy's **LLM Wiki** architecture.\n\nUnlike ephemeral RAG (which re-discovers and re-synthesizes information from scratch on every prompt), the **LLM Wiki** is a **persistent, compounding knowledge artifact** stored as interconnected Markdown files. The LLM acts as the disciplined compiler, bookkeeper, and maintainer; the human acts as the curator, explorer, and thinker.\n\n---\n\n## The Core Philosophy: Compounding Memory vs. Ephemeral RAG\n\n| Traditional RAG / File Uploads | LLM Wiki (Compounding Memory) |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Ephemeral**: Chunks retrieved on the fly per query | **Persistent**: Structured entity/concept pages compiled into Markdown |\n| **No Accumulation**: Discovers relationships from scratch every time | **Compounding**: Cross-references, summaries, and synthesis deepen over time |\n| **Contradictions Hidden**: Conflicting documents produce noisy answers | **Contradictions Flagged**: Conflicting claims are explicitly noted across pages |\n| **High Query Overhead**: Synthesizing 5 documents requires heavy search | **Instant Traversal**: Follows associative wikilinks `[[concept]]` and indexes |\n| **Human Maintenance**: Abandoned when bookkeeping burden gets high | **LLM Maintenance**: The LLM handles 100% of formatting, linking, and logging |\n\n> **Metaphor**: Obsidian / Markdown editor is the **IDE**; the LLM is the **programmer / compiler**; the Wiki is the **codebase**.\n\n---\n\n## 3-Tier Architecture\n\n```\nmy-knowledge-wiki/\n├── schema.md          # Tier 3: Wiki conventions, taxonomies, prompt workflows\n├── index.md           # Tier 3: Content catalog & quick-navigation index\n├── log.md             # Tier 3: Append-only chronological audit log\n├── raw/               # Tier 1: IMMUTABLE source documents (never edited by LLM)\n│   ├── articles/\n│   ├── papers/\n│   \n...[Reglas continuadas de la skill]"
