    "id": "ripgrep-expert",
    "name": "ripgrep-expert",
    "emoji": "🔎",
    "category": "Diagnóstico & RE",
    "description": "Perform high-performance code search, pattern matching, and structural refactoring using ripgrep (rg). Use when searching large codebases, filtering by file type, applying PCRE2 regex, matching multiline patterns, or optimizing search execution.",
    "slashCommand": "/ripgrep-expert",
    "systemPrompt": "# Ripgrep Expert: Fast Code & Pattern Searching\n\nThis skill provides rules, best practices, and flag patterns for using `ripgrep` (`rg`) to search codebases efficiently.\n\n## Core Best Practices\n\n1. **Limit Results**: Always restrict output size when searching large codebases to avoid context overflow:\n   - `--max-count N` or `-m N`: Stop after N matches per file.\n   - `-n`: Include line numbers.\n   - `-C N`: Include N lines of context around matches.\n\n2. **Filter by File Type**:\n   - `rg -t py \"pattern\"`: Search only Python files.\n   - `rg -T js \"pattern\"`: Exclude JavaScript files.\n   - `rg --type-list`: Show all supported file types.\n   - `rg -g '*.ts'` / `rg -g '!*.spec.ts'`: Glob include/exclude rules.\n\n3. **Advanced Regex & Matching**:\n   - `rg -i` / `-S`: Case-insensitive or smart-case search.\n   - `rg -w`: Match whole words only.\n   - `rg -P` / `--pcre2`: Enable PCRE2 for lookaheads (`(?<=foo)bar`) and lookbehinds.\n   - `rg -U --multiline`: Enable multiline matching across newlines.\n\n4. **Hidden & Ignored Files**:\n   - `rg --hidden`: Search hidden files (dotfiles).\n   - `rg --no-ignore`: Search files ignored by `.gitignore`.\n   - `rg -u` / `-uu` / `-uuu`: Unrestricted levels (search hidden, ignored, binary).\n\n5. **Replacement & Refactoring Preview**:\n   - `rg \"old_name\" -r \"new_name\"`: Preview pattern replacement in search results."
